static const char REMOTE_MANIFEST_JSON[] = "{\"builtin\":true,\"caps\":{\"ask\":{\"args\":{\"options\":{\"doc\":\"The choices; blank: Yes and No.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"type\":\"list\"},\"prompt\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"timeout\":{\"default\":60,\"doc\":\"Seconds to wait for an answer.\",\"max\":600,\"min\":5,\"type\":\"int\"}},\"doc\":\"Ask the person holding the remote a question and wait for their answer. The screen shows the prompt and the options; they step through options with the navigation buttons and pick one with OK. Answers {choice, index, button}, or {timeout true} when nobody answered in time.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"bt\":{\"args\":{\"action\":{\"default\":\"status\",\"enum\":[\"status\",\"pair\",\"forget\",\"find\",\"quiet\"],\"type\":\"str\"},\"level\":{\"default\":3,\"max\":3,\"min\":1,\"type\":\"int\"},\"names\":{\"doc\":\"What its keys are called, raw key name (bt_c3) to the name it is sent under (up). Replaces the whole list.\",\"type\":\"map\"}},\"doc\":\"The Bluetooth remote paired to this one (most Android TV remotes). Its keys arrive as remote.button events too, with source bt; a key that means what one of this remote's buttons means has that button's name, any other is bt_c<usage> or bt_k<code>. action pair looks for a remote in pairing mode for 30 seconds and bonds with it; forget drops it; blank answers its state (off, idle, pairing, waiting, connected), name, last raw report, its GATT services and whether it has a microphone the remote can use (voice). find makes a paired remote with a buzzer beep so it can be found (level 1 to 3, quiet to loud; Google's Find My Remote service), quiet stops it; find in the answer says whether it has the service.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"chat\":{\"args\":{\"clear\":{\"default\":false,\"type\":\"bool\"},\"status\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"text\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"who\":{\"default\":\"agent\",\"enum\":[\"you\",\"agent\",\"note\"],\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"The conversation with the house agent on the remote's screen: the last dozen things said, in bubbles (the person's on the right, the agent's on the left, notes bare), scrolled with up and down; the remote's menu has it under Assistant. text adds one, said by who (you: the person, agent, or note), and brings the conversation up; status sets the line under it (Thinking...; blank: none); clear empties it. Answers the conversation as it stands: {messages: [{who, text}]}.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"device\":{\"args\":{\"action\":{\"default\":\"key\",\"enum\":[\"key\",\"launch\",\"power\",\"pair\",\"forget\",\"select\",\"release\"],\"type\":\"str\"},\"app\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"device\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"key\":{\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"Act on a device the scan found, straight from the remote over the local network, no hub in between. device is its id, name or address. action key presses key (up, down, left, right, ok, back, home, menu, vol_up, vol_down, mute, play, pause, rewind, forward, power, or the device's own key name in its own spelling); launch starts app (youtube, netflix, prime, disney, hulu, appletv, plex, or the device's own app id; a Roku also takes an app's name); power turns it off, or wakes it when it is off; pair has an LG TV show its prompt and waits a minute for someone to accept (a Roku needs none); forget drops the pairing; select makes the remote's own buttons drive this device from now on, and release hands them back to the hub's target.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"external\"},\"devices\":{\"doc\":\"What the last scan found, without scanning again, and the device the remote's buttons are driving now (selected), if any.\",\"idempotent\":true,\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"read\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"display\":{\"args\":{\"seconds\":{\"default\":0,\"max\":86400,\"min\":0,\"type\":\"int\"},\"text\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"Show text on the remote's screen (held upright, 16 lines of 5 characters; newlines split lines, long lines wrap). seconds > 0 goes back to the status screen after that long; 0 keeps it until replaced.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"map\":{\"args\":{\"names\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"type\":\"list\"},\"screen_off\":{\"doc\":\"Seconds left alone before the screen goes dark (30; 0: never).\",\"max\":86400,\"min\":0,\"type\":\"int\"},\"sleep\":{\"doc\":\"Seconds left alone before the remote sleeps: Wi-Fi off, so the hub cannot reach it until a key wakes it (300; 0: never).\",\"max\":86400,\"min\":0,\"type\":\"int\"},\"targets\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"type\":\"list\"},\"tz\":{\"doc\":\"The remote's time zone for its clock, as POSIX TZ (CST6CDT,M3.2.0,M11.1.0 for US Central); blank: UTC.\",\"max\":64,\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"Name the buttons and the devices, and say how soon the remote rests. names lists one name per button, in the order remote.state lists them; blank keeps the current names. targets lists the devices the remote's own menu offers (its input button opens it); the one picked there rides every remote.button event as target.\",\"effects\":[\"persists\"],\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"self\"},\"press\":{\"args\":{\"button\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"Press a key as if on the Bluetooth remote paired to this one (up, down, left, right, ok, back, home, input, vol_up...): it does whatever that key does now, in the menu, the game or the conversation, or goes to the device the remote drives. Wakes the remote.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"scan\":{\"doc\":\"Look for devices on the Wi-Fi network the remote has joined (SSDP and mDNS, about 15 seconds) and answer what it found. Each device has an id (its MAC address when known), name, model, address, the kinds it answered as (roku, webos, cast, androidtv, airplay, dial, samsung, wled...), the driver the remote has for it (roku or webos; blank when it can only be seen), what that driver supports, and whether it is paired. The remote also scans on its own a few seconds after joining a network.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"read\",\"scope\":\"external\"},\"screen\":{\"doc\":\"The screen's picture right now: {width, height, rotation (quarter turns clockwise it is shown at), dark (the panel is off), says (the same in words), data}. data is base64 of the panel's own buffer before rotation: one byte for each 8 pixels down a column (lowest bit on top), columns left to right, in bands of 8 rows.\",\"idempotent\":true,\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"read\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"state\":{\"doc\":\"The remote's buttons (names, which are held), the last presses, the device its buttons are for (target, of targets), its mode (remote, menu or game), what the screen shows, Wi-Fi and hub status, the device on its own network it is driving (local), free memory and the firmware update's state.\",\"idempotent\":true,\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"read\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"update\":{\"args\":{\"sha256\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"url\":{\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"Update the remote's firmware over the air. url is where the build is (http or https, reachable from the network the remote is on) and sha256 its SHA-256 in hex; the remote downloads it into its spare slot, checks the hash, answers started and restarts into it. The new build has five minutes to reach the hub, or the remote goes back to the build before. Blank answers the running version, the update's state (idle, downloading, failed, restarting), and whether the build is still on trial.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"exec\",\"scope\":\"self\"},\"wait\":{\"args\":{\"buttons\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"type\":\"list\"},\"timeout\":{\"default\":30,\"doc\":\"Seconds to wait.\",\"max\":600,\"min\":1,\"type\":\"int\"}},\"doc\":\"Wait for the next button press on the remote. Answers {button, action, held_ms}, or {timeout true}. buttons narrows it to those button names.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"read\",\"scope\":\"local\"},\"wifi\":{\"args\":{\"action\":{\"default\":\"list\",\"enum\":[\"list\",\"add\",\"forget\"],\"type\":\"str\"},\"password\":{\"type\":\"str\"},\"ssid\":{\"type\":\"str\"}},\"doc\":\"The Wi-Fi networks the remote knows. Blank lists their names and the one in use. action add saves ssid with password, kept on the device and used when the network in use is out of reach; forget drops ssid. A person can do the same on the remote, in its menu, with its on-screen keyboard.\",\"result\":{\"type\":\"map\"},\"risk\":\"write\",\"scope\":\"self\"}},\"doc\":\"A handheld button remote with a small screen. Button presses arrive as remote.button events; agents can show text on it, ask a question and get the answer from a button press, or wait for the next press.\",\"emits\":{\"remote.button\":{\"doc\":\"A button on the remote was pressed (action press) or held down (action long, once while held). Not sent for the input button (it opens the remote's menu), nor while the menu or the game is up.\",\"payload\":{\"action\":{\"doc\":\"press or long.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"button\":{\"doc\":\"The button's name.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"held_ms\":{\"type\":\"int\"},\"index\":{\"doc\":\"The button's position in remote.state.\",\"type\":\"int\"},\"local\":{\"doc\":\"true when target is a device on the remote's own network that it has already driven itself (remote.device select): nothing is left for a job to do.\",\"type\":\"bool\"},\"source\":{\"doc\":\"bt when the key was pressed on the Bluetooth remote paired to this one.\",\"type\":\"str\"},\"target\":{\"doc\":\"The device picked in the remote's menu (an appliance's name).\",\"type\":\"str\"}}},\"remote.update.check\":{\"doc\":\"Someone picked Update in the remote's menu. The hub's remote-update plugin answers over the band, with remote.update when it holds a newer build for this board.\",\"payload\":{\"board\":{\"doc\":\"bridge-c3 or s3: which build it takes.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"version\":{\"doc\":\"The firmware it runs.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"worker\":{\"doc\":\"This remote's name.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"}}},\"remote.voice\":{\"doc\":\"Someone finished saying something into the microphone of the Bluetooth remote paired to this one (its Assistant key). The audio came before it, in parts remote.voice.part events with the same id.\",\"payload\":{\"bytes\":{\"type\":\"int\"},\"codec\":{\"doc\":\"adpcm8k or adpcm16k: Google's voice-over-BLE frames (ATVV) of IMA ADPCM, mono.\",\"type\":\"str\"},\"id\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"ms\":{\"doc\":\"How long the microphone was open.\",\"type\":\"int\"},\"parts\":{\"doc\":\"How many remote.voice.part events carried it.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"int\"},\"worker\":{\"doc\":\"This remote's name.\",\"type\":\"str\"}}},\"remote.voice.part\":{\"doc\":\"A piece of what is being said (see remote.voice).\",\"payload\":{\"data\":{\"doc\":\"Base64 of the audio bytes the remote sent, in order.\",\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"id\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"str\"},\"seq\":{\"required\":true,\"type\":\"int\"}}}},\"license\":\"Apache-2.0\",\"manifest\":1,\"package\":\"core\",\"plugin\":\"remote\",\"source\":\"https://github.com/Bake-Ware/rook\",\"title\":\"Rook remote\",\"version\":\"0.9.9\"}";
